SN Text Change v2.1

Simple, but effective, way to compare two files and output the changes to
the screen, a file or both.  I use this to compare bbstext changes from
version to version.  There have been many other utilities to do the same
thing, but I wrote this many years ago and it's served me well, so why
change?

Quick & Easy Installation:

 1  Place it somewhere.  (PFiles: would be good.)

 2  At the bottom of the "1; Maintenance" items in bbsmenu, add the
    following line:

    TCHG  |{#0SN:SN_TextChange}

    Modify the path to suit and remember, \ = CTRL-Y and { = CTRL-Q.

 3  Reload your bbstext/bbsmenu via CNet's Control Panel menu (option
    #3, "Text/menu reload  RAmiga-T" and you're all set!

(This sucker wasn't big enough to deserve it's own .guide, installer, icons,
help file, blah blah blah plus tax...)

